  "modules": [
    {
      "id": "uniequip_001_caper",
      "name": {
        "en": "Caper's Badge",
        "zh": "跃跃证章",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "INITIAL",
      "typeName2": "",
      "icon": "uniequip_001_caper",
      "description": {
        "en": "Operator Caper has demonstrated a remarkable aptitude for repeatedly attacking approaching enemies with a boomerang projectile.\nThe Field Operations Department has thus passed the following resolution:\nThis operator shall be appointed a Sniper Operator during field operations to exercise Loopshooter responsibilities.\nIn witness whereof,\nThis is hereby conferred upon the above named.",
        "zh": "干员跃跃擅长操纵回旋投射物往复打击靠近的敌人\n根据外勤部门决议\n在外勤任务中划分为狙击干员，行使回环射手职责\n特别颁发此证章\n以兹证明",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "servers": [
        "cn",
        "global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "uniequip_002_caper",
      "name": {
        "en": "Where the Warmth Remains",
        "zh": "暖意的归宿",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
      "type": "ADVANCED",
      "typeName2": "X",
      "icon": "uniequip_002_caper",
      "description": {
        "en": "It is that time of year again.\nJanuary 20th is the day that Señora Lander cleans up the house, especially her daughter's room, wiping everything clean from the desk to the bed. Ever though her daughter rarely comes back now, she still has had the desk repainted, and the bed sheets changed.\nAfter cleaning, she opens the middle drawer of the desk and takes out a bunch of letters, reading them by the light of her lantern. All of them are letters from Carlie, including the note she left behind when she left home. Señora Lander has kept all of them carefully. The writing of the early letters was childlike and only said that she had found a place where her condition would be treated. There are tear marks from the girl on the first few ones, and Señora Lander finds tears coming to her own eyes every time she sees them.\nSlowly but surely, the writing became smoother and more confident, and the letters started to tell more about Carlie's life: the friends she made, the bad guys she taught a lesson to, and the things she saw outside Bolívar. Through the letters, Señora Lander could almost see her daughter laughing and talking with others—the same lively, fun-loving girl that she had always been.\nIn more recent letters, though, Señora Lander begins to see that her daughter is no longer the child she remembers. Carlie wrote about her thoughts as she received treatment, and the plans that came to mind. She told her mother that she intends to travel throughout Bolívar and beyond, bringing joy to others who suffer from pain and illness, and bravely facing life together. Señora Lander quietly holds the letter in front of her chest, happy at her daughter's growth.\nShe has finished reading all the letters. The lantern is growing dim. She carefully puts the letters away and takes out a fuel canister from the storage room, which is almost the same age as her daughter. She cannot help but smile when she sees the empty cans and 'loops' next to them, that Carlie used to play with. She turns around to look at her daughter's room, knowing that what she is waiting for will soon arrive.\n'You've got mail, Señora Lander!'\nThe mother's heart is warm on this winter's day, as she hears the mailman's voice from outside the door.",
        "zh": "一年一度的这个日子又到了。\n每到一月二十日，兰德女士都会细心地清理整个屋子，特别是女儿的房间，总是要全部整理一遍。从桌子到床铺，兰德女士都擦拭得干干净净。即便女儿已经很少回家，她还是请人给桌子重新上了漆，还在床上铺了全新的床单。\n清洁完毕之后，她打开桌子中间的小抽屉，拿出里面的一叠信件，就着提灯的光从头开始阅读。这些全都是小卡莉写给她的，包括离开家时留下的纸条，兰德女士都小心地珍藏着。一开始的信件笔迹还非常稚嫩，里面除了说找到了治病的地方之外，几乎没有别的信息。最早的几封信上，还能看出小卡莉写信的时候会忍不住掉泪，每次看到那些曾被沾湿的地方，兰德女士就感到眼中也涌出了同样的泪水。\n慢慢地，女儿的笔迹脱掉了稚气，信的内容也变多了。她开始提到自己结交了什么样的朋友，如何教训了不知悔改的恶人，甚至还有她在玻利瓦尔之外的见闻。读着小卡莉的信件，兰德女士总是能想象到女儿和其他人打交道时候的样子。来信之中那些令人莞尔的字句，一再证明着小卡莉还是那个活泼又爱玩的孩子。\n但最近的几次来信，让她觉得女儿不再是自己记忆中的那个孩童了。在信中，小卡莉写下了自己接受治疗以来的一些感想，还有她因此而生的计划。她告诉母亲，她要走遍玻利瓦尔，甚至去更远的地方，给那些一样承受着病痛的人带去快乐，和他们一起勇敢面对生活。兰德女士看到这里，静静地将信放在胸口，知晓自己的孩子已经长大，此刻的她无比安心。\n不知不觉间，兰德女士又看完了所有来信。她望向一边，提灯的火光有些暗淡，里面的燃料已经不多了。她小心地收好信件，走到了储物间。拿出那个几乎和女儿一样年龄的方形燃料罐的时候，她看到了放在一旁的女儿玩过的空罐子和“转转圈”，她不禁微笑起来。她回头看向女儿的房间，她知道很快自己期待的东西又要到了。\n“兰德女士，有你的信！”\n邮递员的声音从门外传来，冬日的小屋里，暖意在母亲的心中流淌……",
        "source": "official",
        "isMachineTranslation": false
      },
